Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:45:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Regulated ZSwap CSL experiment: Stages 0-3 (spend
 relation, gate, ledger matching)

Experiment branch at fa995fa (alexshielded/custom-spend-logic).

- zkir: CSL spend relation (type re-derivation + policy binding, k=15), gate
  relations (authorize, update_root), whitelist helper, prover hook routing
  native relations; legacy relation retained for historical evidence.
- zswap: Input.policy (zswap-input[v3]), verifier reads the binding slot,
  constructor and wallet take token derivation inputs; embedded CSL verifier
  key, legacy key under static/legacy.
- onchain-runtime: effects maps 9 (claimed spend authorizations) and 10
  (claimed output coverage), kernel claim fragments, contract-effects[v5].
- ledger: two-way matching of policy bindings and segment output coverage in
  effects_check; error variants; tag bumps; baseline and scenario tests.
- docs: Stage 1 design decision with as-built notes, results log.

